bg3le static data: reject a false-positive resource manager; never look banks up through bg3se's asserting HashMap

On top of 0001-0008. Two crashes on the first Ext.StaticData read of a run (2026-10-10 18:03:13 log
.1796575; claude-run-2 S060 2026-10-11 09:11:00, 30 s after the 2 h relaunch, log .2717933 l. 729-770):
`static data: resource manager at 0x...eb548 (scanned ...)` -> `Assertion failed: index < size_` -> SIGILL in
bg3se::AssertionFailed <- bg3le_resource_bank <- bg3le_resource_get <- lua_eval_in (debug-port eval).

All 20 logged finds: 18 at region offset 0x15a200 (2 more at 0x15a3c0/0x15aa40) = the real manager; both
crashes found a map at 0xeb5xx, 0x6f000 earlier, whose Keys and Values passed looks_like_manager but whose
HashKeys (bucket heads) point past its Keys, so Definitions.try_get asserted. The recorded offset 0x15a940
never matched, so every run fell back to the scan.

- looks_like_manager also checks the hash structure: every bucket head and NextIds link is -1 or a key index,
  the chains reach every key exactly once (no cycle), NextIds.size == Keys.size, keys distinct.
- bank lookup / count / bank_at read Keys and Values with safe_read and scan the keys (<= 400) instead of
  calling Definitions.try_get / keys() / values()[i] (bg3se asserts = kills the game on a bad index).
- recorded offset 0x15a940 -> 0x15a200.

Offline: tools/test_bg3le_static_data.py compiles hash_chains_hold + read_definitions from the patched source.
Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0008. Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
